{"company":{"id":"stripe","name":"Stripe","accent":"#635bff","asset":"payment intents","verb":"pay"},"nodes":[{"id":"client","title":"Merchant / checkout","kind":"client","blurb":"Card form or wallet button.","depth":0,"story":"This is the Stripe app on your phone or laptop. Tapping pay starts here. The app does not hold the whole product — it only starts the request."},{"id":"api","title":"API / Elements","kind":"api","blurb":"Never put raw cards in your own DB.","depth":1,"story":"Think of this as Stripe’s front desk. The app asks it for “what’s allowed / what’s next,” not for huge payment intents. It routes, limits traffic, and hides internal stores."},{"id":"cdn","title":"CDN","kind":"cdn","blurb":"Checkout.js and static assets.","depth":1,"story":"On Stripe, bulky payment intents are copied around the world. Play/browse should hit a nearby copy. If that copy is missing, a miss goes back to origin."},{"id":"auth","title":"API keys / connect","kind":"auth","blurb":"Which merchant is charging.","depth":2,"story":"Before Stripe shows anything private, it checks who you are (account, session, device). A CDN copy of a file is not the same as being logged in."},{"id":"intent","title":"Payment intent","kind":"service","blurb":"Idempotent charge object.","depth":2,"story":"A payment on Stripe is an object you can retry safely — so a double-tap should not double-charge."},{"id":"risk","title":"Radar / fraud","kind":"service","blurb":"Score the attempt.","depth":2,"story":"Before money moves, Stripe scores “does this look like fraud?” as its own step."},{"id":"vault","title":"Card vault","kind":"service","blurb":"Stores tokens, not raw card numbers.","depth":3,"story":"Card numbers are stored as tokens. Stripe’s logs should not keep raw cards."},{"id":"cache","title":"Idempotency cache","kind":"cache","blurb":"Double-click must not double-charge.","depth":3,"story":"The same questions get asked thousands of times (session, “is this still available?”). Stripe keeps those answers in fast memory so the main database is not hit every time."},{"id":"ledger","title":"Ledger DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Money movement as append-only entries.","depth":4,"story":"The money diary. Append-only facts of what moved — separate from merchant settings."},{"id":"merchdb","title":"Merchant DB","kind":"db","blurb":"Accounts, webhooks, payout schedule.","depth":4,"story":"Shop settings, payout schedule, webhook URLs. Not the ledger of every cent."},{"id":"queue","title":"Webhook queue","kind":"queue","blurb":"Tell the merchant “paid” at-least-once.","depth":5,"story":"Slow leftover work (encode, notify, payout) waits here after you already succeeded at pay. The tap can return; workers finish later."},{"id":"workers","title":"Payout workers","kind":"workers","blurb":"Settle to banks later.","depth":5,"story":"Background helpers at Stripe. They retry if something fails. They are not sitting on the button you just pressed."},{"id":"network","title":"Card networks","kind":"service","blurb":"Visa / bank authorization.","depth":6,"story":"Visa/banks authorize the card. Stripe does not print money; it asks the network."},{"id":"audit","title":"Audit / receipts","kind":"db","blurb":"Compliance trail.","depth":6,"story":"A trail for “what happened.” Needed for disputes and regulators."},{"id":"webhook-delivery","title":"Webhook delivery","kind":"workers","blurb":"Retries merchant notifications safely because the merchant may be offline.","depth":6,"story":"Retries merchant notifications safely because the merchant may be offline."}],"edges":[{"from":"client","to":"cdn","label":"checkout.js"},{"from":"client","to":"api","label":"charge"},{"from":"api","to":"auth","label":"merchant key"},{"from":"api","to":"intent","label":"create intent"},{"from":"intent","to":"risk","label":"fraud score"},{"from":"intent","to":"vault","label":"tokenize card"},{"from":"intent","to":"cache","label":"don’t charge twice"},{"from":"intent","to":"ledger","label":"book entry"},{"from":"intent","to":"network","label":"authorize"},{"from":"intent","to":"queue","label":"webhook later"},{"from":"queue","to":"workers","label":"payout job"},{"from":"workers","to":"merchdb","label":"merchant state"},{"from":"ledger","to":"audit","label":"receipt trail"},{"from":"workers","to":"webhook-delivery","label":"retry webhook"}],"stages":[{"i":0,"blurb":"The checkout page files come from a CDN. The charge itself goes through a payments API—not your shop’s own database.","unlockNodeIds":["client","api","cdn"],"unlockEdgeIds":["client->cdn","client->api","api->auth","api->intent"]},{"i":1,"blurb":"The system knows which shop is charging, creates a payment intent, and scores fraud before money moves.","unlockNodeIds":["auth","intent","risk"],"unlockEdgeIds":["api->auth","api->intent","intent->risk","intent->vault","intent->cache","intent->ledger","intent->network","intent->queue"]},{"i":2,"blurb":"Cards are saved as tokens, not raw numbers. A cache stops a double-click from charging twice.","unlockNodeIds":["vault","cache"],"unlockEdgeIds":["intent->vault","intent->cache"]},{"i":3,"blurb":"A ledger is the money diary. Merchant settings (payouts, webhooks) sit in a different database.","unlockNodeIds":["ledger","merchdb"],"unlockEdgeIds":["intent->ledger","workers->merchdb","ledger->audit"]},{"i":4,"blurb":"“Paid” emails to the shop and bank payouts happen after the tap, in the background.","unlockNodeIds":["queue","workers"],"unlockEdgeIds":["intent->queue","queue->workers","workers->merchdb","workers->webhook-delivery"]},{"i":5,"blurb":"Visa/banks authorize the card. An audit trail keeps a copy of what happened.","unlockNodeIds":["network","audit","webhook-delivery"],"unlockEdgeIds":["intent->network","ledger->audit"]}],"questions":[{"id":"stripe-0-bytes-vs-control-0-0","stage":0,"tid":"bytes-vs-control","variant":0,"correct":"split-paths","distractors":["all-cdn","all-api","all-db"],"seed":2535143418},{"id":"stripe-0-bytes-vs-control-0-1","stage":0,"tid":"bytes-vs-c